@meeting endingTell.go
// SW6 (ending writer A), your answer: GO. As endingTell.stay. Sets end.now.go (EN1), and the kept copy is made the
// first time (spec section 2: SAVE_KEY + '-before-end'). If you'd said Stay before, play endingTell.change.go instead.
title: The Captain
from: Captain Odile Marrow
gist: You told the Captain you're taking the post at headquarters. The Tern leaves Monday, the day after the crossing back.
== lines
marrow: You've come about the letter. Go on. I'm listening.   [listen]
marrow > you: Going. Then we'll make it a proper send-off.   [nod]
marrow: I'll write to headquarters tonight. They'll be very pleased with themselves. Let them be.
? choice
* Was it the right answer?   flavour:listen
  marrow: It was your answer. That's the only kind that's right. You'll be very good there.   [nod]
* I'll miss the Wren.   flavour:share
  marrow: Good. You should. She'll miss you. So will I, and I'm not supposed to say so.   [sigh]
marrow: You can still change your mind until Sunday. Either way, I'm proud of you. Carry on, {me}.
